3. Commercial use is not permitted

No permission is granted under this license for a use primarily intended for
or directed toward commercial advantage, monetary compensation, or the
development or operation of a commercial activity. This includes, without
limitation:

  a. incorporating the covered material into commercial products, services,
     platforms, subscriptions, or other monetized offerings, whether the
     covered material itself is separately charged for or provided free;
  b. using the covered material for internal business operations, commercial
     product development, commercial evaluation, consulting, or paid services;
  c. research, development, or other work commissioned by, sponsored by, or
     conducted in cooperation with a commercial entity for a commercial
     objective, including anticipated commercialization or technology transfer;
  d. selling the covered material or granting others rights to use it for any
     commercial purpose.

These restrictions apply regardless of whether the user is an individual,
company, university, research institute, nonprofit, charity, or government
entity. Institutional status does not create an exception. In particular,
university or research-institute participation does not make commercial
collaboration permissible. Publication of results does not by itself make a
commercially directed activity noncommercial.

Ordinary academic employment and dissemination through scholarly publications
do not, by themselves, make otherwise independent noncommercial research a
commercial activity. However, this clarification does not permit any activity
described in (a) through (d).

Commercial use requires a separate, express, prior written authorization from
the relevant copyright holders. No such authorization is granted by this file.

